+!  JBL: warn if the loop was exhausted without converging, so a
+!  non-converged run doesn't look identical to a converged one in the
+!  output. On normal completion (no "exit" taken) ii = n_up_loop+1; if
+!  "exit" was taken above, ii holds the converged iteration number and
+!  is <= n_up_loop, so this check only fires in the non-converged case.
+  if (ii .gt. n_up_loop) then
